60,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option A sounds chaotic. I don’t want to spend nine minutes finding a desk every day.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option C seems most stable. It minimizes the 6,200 yen re-run costs.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,Option C allows us to assign the window seats deliberately. That addresses the survey.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option C is best for me. I can set up my chair once and leave it.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Yumi,,Option C might isolate the new joiners if they are grouped by function.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Yumi, but if we group by function, maybe the new joiners are in the same group?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, it depends on their roles. But stability is key for the budget.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, we can place the new joiners near the experienced staff in Option C.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, that works. I just need my quiet, ergonomic spot.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, that’s a good point. I’ll consider it.","{""words"":8,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,Option B is too much moving. I hate the idea of shuffling boxes again.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is expensive. Every shift costs 6,200 yen per desk.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,Option B is unpredictable. It doesn’t solve the fairness issue of the window seats.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,Option B is a hassle. I don’t want to re-adjust my chair every few months.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"Option B might help with social mixing, but the cost is too high.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,I’m voting for C. It’s the most stable and addresses the setup time.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I’m voting for C. It’s the most cost-effective and stable.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I’m voting for C. It allows for deliberate, fair assignment of seats.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,I’m voting for C. It’s the most comfortable and least disruptive.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I’m voting for C. It’s the best balance of stability and social connection.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
